# .canaryignore - Gitignore-style patterns for CANARY token scanning
#
# This file specifies files and directories that should be ignored when
# scanning for CANARY tokens. Patterns follow gitignore syntax.
#
# Common patterns:
# - Use # for comments
# - Use / for directory separators
# - Use * for wildcards
# - Use ** for recursive wildcards
# - Use ! to negate patterns (whitelist)
# - Patterns are relative to the root directory

# Template and AI agent configuration directories
.canary/
.claude/
.cursor/
.github/
.windsurf/
.kilocode/
.roo/
.opencode/
.codex/
.augment/
.codebuddy/
.amazonq/

# Documentation directories (often contain example tokens)
# Anchored to root only (CP-285): a bare "docs/"/"specs/" matches ANY
# directory with that name at any depth under gitignore semantics, which
# silently excluded nested dirs like pkg/docs/, pkg/specs/, and
# pkg/cmds/specs/ from scans/upgrades.
/docs/
/specs/

# Build artifacts
bin/
dist/
build/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Dependencies and caches
node_modules/
vendor/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.cache/

# Test data (may contain fixture tokens)
testdata/
fixtures/
test-fixtures/
*_test.go

# Version control
.git/
.direnv/

# Generated files
status.json
status.csv
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Superpowers SDD working files (review diffs contain CANARY-like text)
.superpowers/

# Plugin template/example content (contains example tokens)
claude-plugin/
cursor-plugin/

# Init asset templates: spec-template.md/plan-template.md embed literal
# REQID-XXX example CANARY tokens (with placeholder UPDATED=YYYY-MM-DD dates)
# that specify.go/plan.go substitute via strings.ReplaceAll at generation
# time. They are not real project requirements.
pkg/cmds/init/base/templates/spec-template.md
pkg/cmds/init/base/templates/plan-template.md

# Root README teaching examples (not real tokens)
/README.md
/README_CANARY.md
